From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wig Cheng <onlywig@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:44:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: ethernet: w6300: service interrupts from the monitor
 path

The INT line is configured edge-triggered (GPIO_INT_EDGE_FALLING) and
w6300_handle_interrupts() bails out when an Sn_IR read fails while INT
may still be asserted. No new edge fires in that state, int_sem is
never given again, and the monitor timeout path only updates the link
status: interrupt handling stays disabled permanently.

Run w6300_handle_interrupts() on the monitor period as well. The
handler checks the INT pin first, so this is a no-op while nothing is
pending, and it recovers a missed edge within
CONFIG_ETH_W6300_MONITOR_PERIOD otherwise.

The sibling W5500 driver gained the same kind of protection in commit
d61128427155 ("drivers: eth_w5500: Check W5500 int pin after
processing interrupt").

Signed-off-by: Wig Cheng <onlywig@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c b/drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c
index 43cc11f3b01..9b5392ff571 100644
--- a/drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c
+++ b/drivers/ethernet/eth_w6300.c
@@ -483,7 +483,7 @@ static void w6300_thread(void *p1, void *p2, void *p3)
 			w6300_update_link_status(dev);
 		}
 
-		if (res == 0 && ctx->state.is_up) {
+		if (ctx->state.is_up) {
 			w6300_handle_interrupts(dev, &config->interrupt);
 		}
 	}
